{
  "duration": 90.419,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.019,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.679,
      "end": 2.579,
      "text": "It's time to solve"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.0,
      "end": 3.72,
      "text": "one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.36,
      "end": 5.179,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.819,
      "end": 7.379,
      "text": "we have a ladder of length"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.859,
      "end": 8.5,
      "text": "ten meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.099,
      "end": 10.659,
      "text": "The ladder is making an angle of"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.199,
      "end": 12.079,
      "text": "sixty degrees"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.46,
      "end": 13.039,
      "text": "with the ground."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.479,
      "end": 17.76,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find how high the ladder reaches on the wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.559,
      "end": 18.959,
      "text": "First,"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.34,
      "end": 20.6,
      "text": "let us understand the picture."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.299,
      "end": 22.159,
      "text": "Draw the ground."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.539,
      "end": 23.379,
      "text": "Now draw the wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.219,
      "end": 25.039,
      "text": "Place the ladder"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.579,
      "end": 26.739,
      "text": "leaning against the wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.559,
      "end": 29.879,
      "text": "Since the wall and the ground are perpendicular,"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.539,
      "end": 33.739,
      "text": "this forms a right triangle."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.34,
      "end": 36.119,
      "text": "The ladder is the longest side,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.579,
      "end": 38.359,
      "text": "so it becomes the hypotenuse."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.84,
      "end": 41.239,
      "text": "The height on the wall is the opposite side,"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.759,
      "end": 43.619,
      "text": "and the ground is the adjacent side."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.079,
      "end": 47.439,
      "text": "We already know the hypotenuse, and we need the opposite side."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.979,
      "end": 52.519,
      "text": "So sine theta is the correct trigonometric ratio."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.979,
      "end": 57.519,
      "text": "Sine theta is equal to opposite side divided by hypotenuse."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.02,
      "end": 58.919,
      "text": "Putting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.34,
      "end": 63.079,
      "text": "sine sixty degree is equal to height divided by ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.68,
      "end": 66.559,
      "text": "We also know one standard trigonometric value."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.159,
      "end": 70.879,
      "text": "Sine sixty degree is equal to root three divided by two."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.5,
      "end": 77.459,
      "text": "So the root three divided by two is equal to height divided by ten. Multiply both sides by ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.339,
      "end": 82.219,
      "text": "After simplifying, the height becomes five root three meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.9,
      "end": 83.339,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 83.86,
      "end": 87.879,
      "text": "the ladder reaches a height of five root three meter on the wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.36,
      "end": 90.419,
      "text": "So the correct option is option A"
    }
  ],
